+## B12. Item portraits: `ItemPortrait_<Name>.png`, one per item
+
+Designer note: 120 portraits, more every update, and the detail pane shows one at a time at 128 x 128.
+
+- They are shown one at a time and the set keeps growing, so each portrait is its own image and none go on a sheet.
+- Export each portrait **square, with the corner radius set to 0**, at 2x → **256 x 256**. The 12 px rounding is done in Roblox, so the same file works wherever it is shown.
+- The page has six examples: Torch `40:120`, Ladder `40:121`, Door `40:122`, Fence `40:123`, Chest `40:124`, Bed `40:125`. Export the rest of the 120 the same way.
+
+ImageLabel: `Size = 128 x 128`, `BackgroundTransparency = 1`, `Image =` the item's portrait, `ScaleType = Fit`, plus a `UICorner` with `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 12)`.
